    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76012.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "You know, I was surprised. I was surprised by a couple of things. I was surprised that Garvey was so ill-prepared. But more than that, I was surprised that he made it so personal in our interaction. I challenged him on the lack of a housing policy, the lack of really any specifics. And he got very personal in a way I wasn't expecting. And my sense was, He didn't want to say that he's going to be for Donald Trump. He voted for him twice. He didn't want to say he's going to vote for him again, but he's going to vote for him again. But in order to make sure that he scored points with the MAGA base of Donald Trump, attacking Adam Schiff as the next best thing to pledging your fealty to Donald Trump.",
