    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "This is Donald Trump's argument. This is the no collusion, no obstruction mantra of Trump. The facts are very different. As I laid out during the debate, Donald Trump's campaign chairman was secretly meeting with Russian intelligence and giving them their internal polling data while Russian intelligence was helping their campaign. Everybody other than Donald Trump recognizes, okay, that's certainly collusion. Can you imagine, Alex, if Hillary Clinton's campaign manager was meeting with Russian intelligence and giving them information so they could help her campaign, they would be screaming collusion from the rafters. So, Garvey there is being dishonest, but look, he's carrying the water for Donald Trump. This censure was a partisan censure, and Donald Trump made sure it would pass by threatening anyone who voted against it with being a primary, suffering a primary challenge.",
