    "turn_text": "to you. Well, and I'm very proud to have losing endorsement, and not only losing endorsement, but now the endorsement of every other Orange County representative of Congress other than Katie Porter has endorsed my campaign. It's not all about earmarks. I think, frankly, bringing back money to California is indicative of something broader, which is Is the senator going to fight to help Californians? We're a donor state. We send much more back to Washington than we get back as Californians. Any senator who says, I'm not going to do that when every other senator in the country is, is saying basically, I'd rather that money go to New York. I'd rather go to Ted Cruz in Texas. I'd rather go anywhere but California. My constituents, they'd rather have housing and a roof over their head than a political talking point, whether it's farmers in the Central Valley with the need for water infrastructure. I'm going to do what Dianne Feinstein did, which is bring back billions. I'm going to do what Alex Padilla is doing, which is bring back millions and billions. I'm going to make sure that I'm doing everything to meet the needs of Californians, not just a poll-driven talking point.",
