    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76012.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "First of all, if he becomes president, I think we're in deep trouble. This is someone who says he's going to be a dictator in day one. But more than that, what I've demonstrated throughout my time in Congress is even in the most difficult times, there's still ways to work together on the intelligence committee where Devin Nunes and I fought cats and dogs over Russia and Ukraine and presidential abuse of power. Every year, we still got our intelligence authorization bills done. We did every year the work of the intelligence committee because we had to decide, OK, we're not going to let these other differences get in the way of getting things done. I worked with Republican Dave Dryer on mass transit. I worked with Republican John Culberson on funding NASA and our space exploration. I have a long record of working across the aisle to get things done, and I'll continue to do that.",
