    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, you have to have a partner on the other side of the aisle that actually wants to get something done. Right now, as you point out, Don Trump is telling Republicans don't work with Democrats to solve this problem. If you don't have a partner on the other side of the aisle, then you darn well need to make sure that when you control both sides, House and Senate, that you get the job done yourself. And frankly, when Democrats have been in charge of both houses, we haven't gotten the job done, and that's on us.",
