    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "There is a crisis at the border. You know, there are lots of people coming, fleeing violence, seeking a better life. And the best thing we could do, I think, is make it possible and safe for people to apply for asylum in their home countries. Now, that's not always possible, but it's infinitely preferable to people making that dangerous journey to the country, and then having to wait years and years for their claim to be processed, their petition. We do need for those who do come to the country to be able to move much more quickly in assessing these asylum petitions. Are they valid? Are they not? It's not good for people to wait in limbo for years, and it's not good for the country. We need more resources for communities that are impacted, but I'll tell you what we don't need anymore of. We don't need any more of treating these folks as political pods, putting them on buses and planes, making a spectacle out of their desperation. They deserve our dignity and they deserve our respect.",
